    "report_markdown": "# Hypora run report: run_923aeadb28b4\n\n**Outcome:** a verified model.\n\n## Task\n- Objective: Predict whether a credit applicant is a good or bad customer so underwriters can use the score when deciding on an application.\n- Target: `good_or_bad_customer` (binary_classification)\n- Primary metric: `roc_auc` (maximize)\n\n## Summary\nThe run aimed to predict whether a credit applicant is a good or bad customer, to support underwriters\u2019 decisions. It compared a regularized logistic regression baseline with several tree-based alternatives using stratified validation. The verified logistic regression model was delivered, with test performance summarized by 0.9651.\n\n**Observations**\n- The selected model\u2019s mean validation ROC AUC was 0.9679.\n- The selected model\u2019s test accuracy was 0.9133, and its test recall was 0.9619.\n- The logistic regression baseline was selected over the tested tree-based candidates.\n\n**Limitations**\n- A leakage candidate was flagged among the screened features and requires methodological review; leakage has not been ruled out.\n- The learned-transform leakage check was skipped, so this aspect was not verified.\n- The scores describe this evaluation setup and do not establish performance or suitability for real underwriting decisions.\n\n_Written by the Reporter; every number above is filled in from stored metrics._\n\n## Final model\n- Trial `trl_093627db`: A regularized logistic regression with one-hot categorical encoding provides a stable baseline for the small mixed-type credit dataset.\n- Verified: yes\n\n| Metric | Test (once) | Validation (mean) |\n|---|---|---|\n| roc_auc | 0.9651 | 0.9679 |\n| accuracy | 0.9133 | 0.9317 |\n| balanced_accuracy | 0.8810 | 0.9004 |\n| precision | 0.9182 | 0.9278 |\n| recall | 0.9619 | 0.9786 |\n| f1 | 0.9395 | 0.9525 |\n| precision_macro | 0.9091 | 0.9352 |\n| recall_macro | 0.8810 | 0.9004 |\n| f1_macro | 0.8933 | 0.9154 |\n| pr_auc | 0.9818 | 0.9846 |\n| log_loss | 0.1988 | 0.1880 |\n| brier_score | 0.0602 | 0.0547 |\n\n| Check | Status | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| allowed_features | passed | trial code received exactly the contract's allowed features |\n| split_respected | passed | stratified split: disjoint, complete |\n| test_labels_not_accessed | passed | every predict stage saw features and the model only |\n| output_shape | passed | one prediction per planned row, task-shaped columns |\n| finite_outputs | passed | all predictions finite and well-formed |\n| metric_recomputation | passed | recomputed metrics match the harness |\n| artifact_loads | passed | the frozen model loaded in a sandbox and predicted the test split |\n| resource_limits | passed | every stage completed inside the submitted job's limits |\n| learned_transform_leakage | skipped | static analysis of fit/predict arrives with verifier v2 (S3.C4) |\n\n## Trials\n| Trial | Kind | Status | Validation roc_auc (mean \u00b1 std, folds) | Hypothesis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `trl_093627db` | baseline | verified | 0.9679 \u00b1 0.0028 (3) | A regularized logistic regression with one-hot categorical encoding provides a stable baseline for the small mixed-type credit dataset. |\n| `trl_ca188731` | candidate | validated | 0.9667 \u00b1 0.0076 (3) | A regularized histogram gradient-boosting model over one-hot categorical and scaled numeric features captures nonlinear credit-risk interactions while controlling complexity on a small dataset. |\n| `trl_f627ee7c` | candidate | validated | 0.9672 \u00b1 0.0053 (3) | Shallow stochastic gradient-boosted trees on the encoded inputs may exploit the exceptionally strong flagged collections signal and complementary nonlinearities better than the linear baseline without allowing deep-tree overfit. |\n| `trl_fae3776a` | candidate | validated | 0.9505 \u00b1 0.0018 (3) | An ExtraTrees ensemble with shallowish trees can rank applicants by nonlinear interactions and heterogeneous category effects with relatively low variance. |\n\n## Data\n- Split: stratified, 20% test, stratified_kfold_3\n- Features used: 21; excluded: none\n- Leakage screen: Leakage candidates flagged: 1 among 21 screened features; methodological review is required.\n\n## Decision and faults\n- Decision: train (approved_plan)\n\n## Run notes\n- Stage-1 placeholder (D-019): contract built by code, plan approved by policy; replaced by the Data Lead (S3.A2) and the plan gate (S3.D2).\n- The agent finished after 14 model turns, 18 tool calls; it nominated trl_093627db.\n- Final candidate trl_093627db: nominated by the agent.\n- Final job job_1794152557043008688_32f4e5: test split scored once; verifier v1 passed.\n\n## Sources\n- `task_spec:run_923aeadb28b4.v1`\n- `profile:run_923aeadb28b4.profile.2a2a607e2871`\n- `experiment_contract:run_923aeadb28b4.v1`\n- `result:trl_093627db/test`\n"
  },
